## Decisions
The new tool is labs/colab-workflow-pass02. Accepted labs/colab-workflow-pass01 stays in place. This tool calls the pinned v2 producer `verify`. It does not call handoff_check.py. A change that full verify rejects is conflicting bytes, including an identity change that the held standalone checker would miss.

Attach copies package bytes, the ZIP, and verification.json. It writes 05.NN.pack.md as those exact pack bytes. It stores the preparation notes as those exact bytes under the pass artifacts. The page file 06.NN.notes.md is a projection: a length-prefixed launch snapshot, then append-only working lines. An append does not change the stored snapshot or the package digest.

05.NN.return.md is written only by place-return, and only as the exact return.md bytes from a verified capture. Member, receipt, and return sha256 are a separate record and the 08.md projection. The return file does not gain a provenance footer.

06.NN.review.md is rendered only from a supplied review record after the return is placed. A missing director reply refuses. The tool does not fill one in. Routes are hold, finish, request-next, and route-n5nn. request-next records the caller-named next pass and does not create that pack. finish is not approval. Unresolved findings stay in the review projection.

One pass holds one package, one return, and one review. The same bytes are a readonly repeat. Different bytes stay refused and the previous bytes remain. This tool does not reserve, capture, allocate a member, or allocate a next pass.

The live work book stays refused as the book. The tool does not write 00.live. Source paths may name 0411.colab or a file 07.md. The tool still does not create face 07 or a filename ending in .colab.

